This method does not compile on any C# version (C# 13 and later report CS4007, `Span<byte>` cannot be preserved across an `await`, plus CS1503 on the `ReadAsync` call; C# 12 rejects the `ref struct` local in an async method outright):

```csharp
async Task<string> ReadHeaderAsync(Stream s)
{
    Span<byte> buf = stackalloc byte[64];
    int n = await s.ReadAsync(buf);
    return Encoding.ASCII.GetString(buf[..n]);
}
```

Which change makes it compile and behave correctly?

